  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 305 AM EDT Mon Aug 24 2026\n\nAfter a drier and more pleasant early week, moisture will be \nincreasing ahead of an approaching cold front by midweek. Dewpoints \nwill surge back toward the 70s by Wednesday into Thursday. PoPs will \ninitially begin to increase by late Wednesday as a shortwave \ndisturbance initiates thunderstorm development to our west/northwest \nthat could approach the area by Wednesday evening into Wednesday \nnight. The most substantial increase in PoPs will be by Thursday, \nhowever, as the aforementioned front pushes into the area, lingering \ninto late week. With PWATs surging back over 2\" in advance of the \nfront, locally heavy rainfall could be a concern during this time.\n\nAs far as temperatures are concerned, 60s will remain abundant for \nmorning lows for much of north Georgia through the bulk of the \nperiod. Highs will range from the upper 80s to lower 90s, within a \nfew degrees of seasonal normals for the most part.",
